---
# Advisory for now: CI runs clang-tidy without failing the build while the
# existing backlog is worked down (see ROADMAP.md, "Clear the clang-tidy
# backlog"). Do not add new findings. WarningsAsErrors is deliberately empty
# until the backlog is zero, at which point it becomes '*' and the gate turns
# blocking -- the same rule the sanitisers already follow: a baseline with a
# remembered exception is one nobody reads carefully.
#
# The disabled checks below are switched off for a reason, not to flatter the
# number. Everything in the first group is stylistic preference that would fight
# JUCE and audio idiom -- C arrays are how you address a sample buffer, and
# `[[nodiscard]]` on 261 accessors is noise, not safety. Everything kept can
# point at a real defect: narrowing conversions and misplaced widening casts
# matter a great deal in code that does sample arithmetic.
Checks: >
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -modernize-use-auto,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -readability-named-parameter

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '^.*/(src|test|tools)/[^/]*\.h$'
...
